{"repositoryId":1407258340,"availability":"available","full":"unixzii/synth-ui","name":"synth-ui","description":"A TypeScript library for building pixel-art user interfaces.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":26,"forks":2,"created":"2026-10-06T12:24:56Z","updated":"2026-10-06T13:09:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://synth-ui-demo.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://synth-ui-demo.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.092Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.092Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.092Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.092Z","stars":26,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A TypeScript library for building pixel-art user interfaces. Everything is drawn at a low resolution, in whole pixels and from a small palette, the way 8-bit hardware drew, and then shown on screen with an optional CRT glow and scanlines. The UI is written in immediate mode: each frame, plain code draws the whole interface and asks each control what happened to it, so there are no widget objects to create, update or keep in sync with the app's data.","It comes with a set of controls suited to tools and instruments (buttons, knobs, sliders, text fields, lists, menus, sheets) in a warm, retro look: warm greys, one orange accent, and bloom on what's lit. Synthez, for example, draws its whole interface with it."],"features":["Immediate mode. The draw code is the UI. Controls return what happened","(clicked, the new value, the text typed) instead of taking callbacks.","Real pixels. Rendering is to an 8-bit indexed surface: colours are","palette indices, and fades, tints and shadows are colour maps with ordered dither. Filters (ramps, vignettes), mosaic and remapping work on what's already drawn.","A CRT look. The GPU simulates the tube, through wgpu (WebGPU on the"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/unixzii/synth-ui/blob/main/README.m